(its centerline \(180 deg cut\). Shows complete interior.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Half Section: Used for symmetrical objects. Cutting plane cuts halfway through) Tj
T*
(\(90 deg cut\). One half is drawn in section showing interior, while the other half) Tj
T*
(remains as an exterior view showing outside profile. No hidden lines needed on either) Tj
T*
(half unless essential for dimensioning.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Offset Section: Cutting plane bends at 90-degree right angles to pass through) Tj
T*
(non-collinear features \(e.g., passing through a central hub, stepping down to pass) Tj
T*
(through an offset mounting hole\). The 90-degree transition offsets are NOT shown with) Tj
T*
(lines in the sectional view.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Revolved Section: Cross-section of a feature \(bar, spoke, rib\) rotated 90) Tj
T*
(degrees in place onto the longitudinal view.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Removed Section: Cross-section displaced away from the view and placed nearby) Tj
T*
(with clear identification callout \(e.g., Section B-B\).) Tj
T*
(* 6. Broken-Out / Local Section: Small partial section bounded by an irregular) Tj
T*
(freehand line to expose an isolated interior detail.) Tj
