(>> 4.4 AutoCAD Editing and Hatching Commands) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* STRETCH \(S\): Select vertices with crossing window \(green window\); moves vertices) Tj
T*
(while maintaining connectivity of attached geometry.) Tj
T*
(* EXPLODE \(X\): Breaks compound objects \(Polylines, Blocks, Dimensions, Regions\) into) Tj
T*
(basic independent constituent lines and arcs.) Tj
T*
(* OFFSET \(O\): Creates parallel concentric curves or parallel lines at a designated) Tj
T*
(offset distance or through point.) Tj
T*
(* JOIN \(J\): Merges collinear line segments, connected polyline segments, or) Tj
T*
(continuous spline curves into a single entity.) Tj
T*
(* REGION \(REG\): Converts an enclosed 2D boundary loop into a 2D planar solid surface) Tj
T*
(with geometric and physical properties.) Tj
T*
(* BREAK \(BR\): Breaks a line or arc between two selected points, creating a gap or) Tj
T*
(dividing into two entities.) Tj
T*
(* HATCH \(H\): Fills enclosed boundaries with pattern \(ANSI31 standard 45 deg lines,) Tj
T*
(Solid, User-defined\). Properties: Pattern, Scale, Angle, Associativity.) Tj
T*
(* HATCHEDIT \(HE\): Modifies pattern type, density scale, or island detection of) Tj
T*
(existing hatch objects.) Tj
T*
