(Problem Statement: A gearbox cover plate \(200 mm x 120 mm x 20 mm\) has a central shaft) Tj
T*
(bearing hole \(dia 50 mm\) and two mounting bolt holes \(dia 14 mm\) located offset from the) Tj
T*
(centerline. Illustrate the path of the cutting plane and resulting Offset Section) Tj
T*
(A-B-C-D.) Tj
T*
(Engineering Solution:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Cutting Plane Line on Plan View: Enters left edge along line of sight, steps) Tj
T*
(forward by 30 mm at a 90 deg corner to pass through the first bolt hole, steps back) Tj
T*
(along the center axis to slice through the central bearing hole, and steps out) Tj
T*
(through the second bolt hole.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Sectional View Representation: Drawn as a continuous uninterrupted flat) Tj
T*
(sectional view. The right-angled step transitions are completely invisible in the) Tj
T*
(sectioned view.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Both the bolt holes and central shaft hole appear as full open cavities with) Tj
T*
(hatched metal around them.) Tj
T*
