([PROBLEM 4: AutoCAD Hatching and Region Creation Tutorial]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Create associative hatch patterns and modify hatch density for a) Tj
T*
(cross-sectional engine piston drawing.) Tj
T*
(AutoCAD Command Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. BOUNDARY / REGION: Type REGION -> Select all boundary lines of the section cut) Tj
T*
(-> Press Enter. Verify command line confirms: "1 loop extracted, 1 Region created".) Tj
T*
(* 2. HATCH -> Type H -> Select ANSI31 \(standard 45 deg iron hatch\) -> Set Scale: 1.5) Tj
T*
(-> Select Pick Points inside region.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Verify Associativity: Move boundary vertex with STRETCH command; observe that) Tj
T*
(the Hatch pattern automatically dynamically updates and conforms to the new boundary.) Tj
T*
(* 4. HATCHEDIT: Type HE -> Select hatch -> Change Angle to 135 degrees for adjacent) Tj
T*
(mating sleeve; change scale to 2.0 to differentiate parts.) Tj
T*
